# PuckRacer Coordinator — Architecture Index
# Last updated: 2026-04-29

## SYSTEM OVERVIEW
ESP32-S3 coordinator that manages wireless LED pucks via ESP-NOW for sports/training games.
- IP: 192.168.42.1 | SSID: PuckRace_Trainer (no password)
- Captive Portal: any DNS → 192.168.42.1
- Single-user lock ("Türsteher"): 45s timeout, one active client at a time
- Platform: PlatformIO, Arduino framework, ESP-IDF 5.x
- Filesystem: LittleFS (serves HTML/JS/CSS to browser)
- No PSRAM usage (clone compatibility issues)
- Version: defined as SYSTEM_VERSION in main.cpp
- Status-LED Ring: 16x WS2812B an GPIO 4 (Lila Boot / Gelb idle / Grün connected)

## BOOT SEQUENCE (main.cpp)
1. StatusLed::begin() — WS2812B Ring (16 LEDs an GPIO 4), Lila als Boot-Indikator
2. LittleFS.begin() — mount filesystem
3. activationManager.begin() — load/validate license
4. PuckNetwork::begin() — WiFi AP + ESP-NOW init
5. WebHandler::begin() — AsyncWebServer + DNS
6. GameManager::begin() — StatsManager init

## MAIN LOOP (main.cpp)
PuckNetwork::update() → WebHandler::update() → GameManager::update() → WifiScanner::loop() → StatusLed::update()

